course: dictionary
lesson: 15490
title: Strung and its many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Strung» is a form of the verb «string», which means to put things on a thread, cord or line. Yesterday Mia strung red and blue beads onto a thread to make a bracelet. Today the beads are strung.
explain: The same word can mean different things. «The workers strung fairy lights across the street for the party.» Here strung means hung up on a line, so the lights hang from one side of the street to the other.
explain: Read the words around it to choose the meaning. Beads, lights or flags point to threading or hanging. A guitar or a tennis racket points to strings being fitted. «Sam felt highly strung before the test» means Sam was easily upset and nervous.
fact: «Strung» is the past form of «string»: string, strings, strung, stringing.
fact: «Strung» can mean beads put on a thread one after another.
fact: «Strung» can mean hung up on a string or line, like lights or flags.
fact: A strung instrument or racket has its strings fitted.
fact: «Highly strung» means easily upset or nervous, and «strung out» can mean spread out in a long line.
exercise: «Ava strung red and yellow beads onto a thread.» What did Ava do? | Counted the beads by colour | *Put the beads on a thread one after another | Lost the beads in the grass | Painted the beads gold
exercise: «Dad strung flags across the garden for the party.» What does strung mean here? | Folded into a neat box | Sewn onto a jacket | *Hung up on a line | Washed in the rain
exercise: «Sam felt highly strung before the spelling test.» What does highly strung mean? | Full of energy and running fast | Happy and calm | Very tall and strong | *Easily upset and nervous
test: «The guitar was strung with new strings before the concert.» What does strung mean here? | Lost under a bed | *Had its strings fitted | Put into a box | Hung up on a wall
test: «The runners were strung out along the track after the race.» What does strung out suggest? | Hidden behind the bushes | *Spread out in a long line | Shouting at the referee | Sleeping under the trees
exam: Which sentence uses strung to mean easily upset? | The necklace was strung with shiny pearls | *Our goalkeeper is highly strung and gets upset very easily | The flags were strung across the playground
